  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-0.6)=-36.869\\,897\u2026\u2248-36.8699\n$$\n\nSince $-{36.8699}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-{36.8699}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={36.8699}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={36.8699}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977985/assets/8d88b4ccfe08c26c9d56effaf651e04703995ffaec4b7ab08187f62ddd1897de.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={180}^{\u2218}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}+{36.8699}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={216.8699}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we subtract ${360}^{\u2218}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=X-{360}^{\u2218} & ={216.8699}^{\u2218}-{360}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =-{143.1301}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx\u2248-{143.1}^{\u2218},\\,x\u2248-{36.9}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
